Scope: the code, not the person behind it
-----------------------------------------

This repository is my job application. The MIT license above covers the
machinery — take it, change it, build your own site with it:

  src/components/   src/layouts/   src/pages/   src/styles/   src/data/bild.ts
  public/js/        public/_headers   tools/    astro.config.mjs
  wrangler.jsonc    .github/       package.json

It does NOT cover the content, which is mine personally and is published here
so people can read it, not reuse it. All rights reserved for:

  src/data/inhalt.ts        every text on the site
  src/data/revisionen.json  the change history
  src/assets/media/         screenshots, my photograph
  public/media/             image variants, the clips, the link preview
  public/dokumente/         my CV and my (redacted) references
  public/daten/             Wordle's own word lists, see below
  DESIGN.md                 the design system as a document
  README.md, PRODUCT.md     the write-ups

Two further points, because not everything here is mine to give away:

- The screenshots and the clip on sheet M-1, and the four-line code excerpt
  beside them, show software built for Projektron GmbH. They are published
  with their permission; the code belongs to the client. The clip and the
  stills of it are not licensed for reuse.
- The artwork and sound on sheet M-2 were made by the Kaiju Adventure project
  team and are shown with their permission. They remain theirs.
- `public/daten/wordle-*.txt` are Wordle's own word lists, taken from public
  collections (github.com/tabatkins/wordle-list). Wordle is a trademark of
  The New York Times Company; this site is not affiliated with them.

If you want to reuse something and are unsure which side of the line it falls
on, write to me: abdilkarimb@gmail.com
